sn4.4:4.1 | S: “I’m freed from Māra’s snares, | T: The Blessed One: “I am freed from Mara’s snare
sn4.4:4.2 | S: both human and heavenly. | T: Both celestial and human;
sn4.4:4.3 | S: I’m freed from Māra’s bonds. | T: I am freed from Mara’s bondage:
sn4.4:4.4 | S: You’re beaten, terminator!” | T: You’re defeated, End-maker!”
sn4.4:5.1 | S: Then Māra … vanished right there. | T: Then Mara the Evil One … disappeared right there.

## sn4.7
sn4.7:1.1 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. | T: On one occasion the Blessed One was dwelling at Rajagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the Squirrel Sanctuary.
sn4.7:1.2 | S: He spent much of the night walking mindfully in the open. At the crack of dawn he washed his feet and entered his dwelling. | T: Then, when the night was fading, the Blessed One, having spent much of the night walking back and forth in the open, washed his feet, entered his dwelling,
sn4.7:1.3 | S: He laid down in the lion’s posture—on the right side, placing one foot on top of the other—mindful and aware, and focused on the time of getting up. | T: and lay down on his right side in the lion’s posture, with one leg overlapping the other, mindful and clearly comprehending, having attended to the idea of rising.
sn4.7:1.4 | S: Then Māra the Wicked went up to the Buddha and addressed him in verse: | T: Then Mara the Evil One approached the Blessed One and addressed him in verse:
sn4.7:2.1 | S: “What, you’re asleep? <j>Really, you’re asleep? | T: “What, you sleep? Why do you sleep?
sn4.7:2.2 | S: You sleep like a loser—<j>what’s up with that? | T: What’s this, you sleep like a wretch?
sn4.7:2.3 | S: You sleep, thinking that the hut is empty. | T: Thinking ‘The hut’s empty’ you sleep:
sn4.7:2.4 | S: You sleep when the sun has come up—<j>what’s up with that?” | T: What’s this, you sleep when the sun has risen?”
sn4.7:3.1 | S: “For them there is no craving— | T: The Blessed One: “Within him craving no longer lurks,
sn4.7:3.2 | S: the weaver, the clinger—<j>to track them anywhere. | T: Entangling and binding, to lead him anywhere;
sn4.7:3.3 | S: With the ending of all attachments <j>the awakened Buddha sleeps. | T: With the destruction of all acquisitions The Awakened One sleeps:
sn4.7:3.4 | S: What’s that got to do with you, Māra?” | T: Why should this concern you, Mara?”
sn4.7:4.1 | S: Then Māra … vanished right there. | T: Then Mara the Evil One … disappeared right there.

## sn4.8
sn4.8:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: Thus have I heard.
sn4.8:1.2 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. | T: On one occasion the Blessed One was dwelling at Savatthi in Jeta’s Grove, Anathapiṇḍika’s Park.
sn4.8:1.3 | S: Then Māra the Wicked went up to the Buddha and spoke this verse in the Buddha’s presence: | T: Then Mara the Evil One approached the Blessed One and recited this verse in the presence of the Blessed One:
