## sn45.10
sn45.10:1.1 | S: At Sāvatthī. | T: At Savatthī.
sn45.10:1.2 | S: Then the wanderer Nandiya went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. | T: Then the wanderer Nandiya approached the Blessed One and exchanged greetings with him.
sn45.10:1.3 | S: When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side, and said to the Buddha: | T: When they had concluded their greetings and cordial talk, he sat down to one side and said to the Blessed One:
sn45.10:1.4 | S: “Worthy Gotama, how many things, when developed and cultivated, have extinguishment as their target, destination, and culmination?” | T: “How many things, Master Gotama, when developed and cultivated, lead to Nibbāna, have Nibbāna as their destination, Nibbāna as their final goal?”
sn45.10:2.1 | S: “These eight things, when developed and cultivated, have extinguishment as their target, destination, and culmination. | T: “These eight things, Nandiya, when developed and cultivated, lead to Nibbāna, have Nibbāna as their destination, Nibbāna as their final goal.
sn45.10:2.2 | S: What eight? | T: What eight?
sn45.10:2.3 | S: They are: right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion. | T: Right view … right concentration.
sn45.10:2.4 | S: These eight things, when developed and cultivated, have extinguishment as their target, destination, and culmination.” | T: These eight things, when developed and cultivated, lead to Nibbāna, have Nibbāna as their destination, Nibbāna as their final goal.”
sn45.10:2.5 | S: When he said this, the wanderer Nandiya said to the Buddha, | T: When this was said, the wanderer Nandiya said to the Blessed One:
sn45.10:2.6 | S: “Excellent, worthy Gotama! Excellent! … | T: “Magnificent, Master Gotama! Magnificent, Master Gotama!…
sn45.10:2.7 | S: From this day forth, may the worthy Gotama remember me as a lay follower who has gone for refuge for life.” | T: From today let Master Gotama remember me as a lay follower who has gone for refuge for life.”
sn45.10:2.8 | P: Dasamaṁ. | T: (none)
sn45.10:2.9 | P: Avijjāvaggo paṭhamo. | T: (none)
