sn45.146-148:3.1 | S: “Mendicants, cloth from Kāsi is said to be the best kind of woven cloth. …” | T: The Cloth “Bhikkhus, just as, of all woven cloths, Kasian cloth is declared to be their chief,
sn45.146-148:3.2 | P: evameva kho, bhikkhave, ye keci kusalā dhammā, sabbe te appamādamūlakā appamādasamosaraṇā; | T: so too whatever wholesome states there are, they are all rooted in diligence, converge upon diligence,
sn45.146-148:3.3 | P: appamādo tesaṁ dhammānaṁ aggamakkhāyati. | T: and diligence is declared to be the chief among them.
sn45.146-148:3.4 | P: Appamattassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—ariyaṁ aṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ bhāvessati ariyaṁ aṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ bahulīkarissati. | T: When a bhikkhu is diligent, it is to be expected that he will develop and cultivate the Noble Eightfold Path.
sn45.146-148:3.5 | P: Kathañca, bhikkhave, bhikkhu appamatto ariyaṁ aṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ bhāveti ariyaṁ aṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ bahulīkaroti? | T: “And how, bhikkhus, does a bhikkhu who is diligent develop and cultivate the Noble Eightfold Path?
sn45.146-148:3.6 | P: Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu sammādiṭṭhiṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe… sammāsamādhiṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe… | T: Here, bhikkhus, a bhikkhu develops right view … right concentration, which is based upon seclusion, dispassion, and cessation, maturing in release.
sn45.146-148:3.7 | P: evaṁ kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu appamatto ariyaṁ aṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ bhāveti ariyaṁ aṭṭhaṅgikaṁ maggaṁ bahulīkarotī”ti. | T: It is in this way, bhikkhus, that a bhikkhu who is diligent develops and cultivates the Noble Eightfold Path.”
